5. Estimation and Overhead Reality

Reuse probability  \hat{R}_i . Estimated via an exponential moving average (EMA) of access inter‑arrival times. To handle abrupt phase changes (e.g., prefill to decode in LLMs), we maintain two windows (short and long). When the ratio of short‑term to long‑term frequency exceeds a threshold, the predictor resets or increases the adaptation gain. However, this EMA‑reset heuristic currently has no formal regret bound; its sample complexity under non‑stationary Zipf workloads is an open question.

Recomputation cost  C_i . Profiled offline from layer shapes or extracted from computation graph metadata.

Energy and bandwidth coefficients. Derived from hardware datasheets as first‑order approximations. Online refinement via a lightweight system identification loop is expected to be necessary for deployment.

Coefficients  \alpha, \beta, \gamma, \delta  are absent from the final MVF form; they are absorbed into the unit‑conversion factor  \phi_B  and the shadow prices. The policy thus depends only on physically meaningful quantities and on the Lagrange multipliers that the system adjusts automatically.

